          %p
            The pivotal role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (
            %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#fn:1"}> Lawvere 08
            ) and in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adjointness+in+Foundations"}> Lawvere 69
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohesive+Toposes+and+Cantor%27s+lauter+Einsen"} Lawvere 94
            ) was particularly amplified by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+W.+Lawvere"} F. W. Lawvere
            = succeed "." do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere
            saw the future of category theory (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+Thoughts+on+the+Future+of+Category+Theory"}> Lawvere 91
            ) as concerned with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            expressing systems of archetypical dualities that reveal foundations for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "cohesive+topos#LawvereAxiomatic"}> Lawvere 07
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes+of+laws+of+motion"}> Lawvere 97
            , see Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohesiveTopos"}
            and Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialCohesion"}
            below). He suggested (
            %a{:href => "objective+and+subjective+logic#Lawvere94"}> Lawvere 94
            ) this as a precise formulation of core aspects of the
            %em theory of everything
            of early 19th century
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hegel"} Hegel
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Science+of+Logic"} Science of Logic
          %p
            These days, of course,
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories+of+everything"} theories of everything
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} of particle physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} of cosmology
            to a more coherent whole.
          %p
            The idea of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            refers to different perspectives on physics that appear dual to each other while being
            = succeed "." do
              %em equivalent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EveryEquivalenceOfCategoriesComesFromAnAdjointEquivalence"}
          %p
            Of course the usage of the term
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            is too loose for one to expect to be able to refine each occurrence of the term in the literature to a mathematical adjunction. However, we will see mathematical formalizations of core aspects of key string-theoretic dualities, such as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualities+in+string+theory"} dualities in string theory
            is the phenomenon of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            along the point inclusion into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} fundamental super p-branes
          %p This suggests that there may be a deeper relation here between the superficially alien uses of the word “duality”, that is worth exploring.
          %p
            In this respect it is worth noticing that core structure of string/M-theory arises via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            (as explained in the chapter
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} on fundamental super p-branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            (explained in the chapter
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} on supergeometry
          %p
