          %div
            %h2#BasicNotionsOfCategoryTheory Basic notions of Category theory
            %p
              We introduce here the basic notions of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#CategoriesAndFunctors"} Categories and functors
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#NaturalTransformationsAndPresheaves"} Natural transformations and presheaves
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#Adjunctions"} Adjunctions
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#Equivalences"} Equivalences
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#Modalities"} Modalities
            %p
              This constitutes what is sometimes called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em language of categories
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaLemma"}
              below), what makes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              be a
              %em mathematical theory
              in the sense of a coherent collection of non-trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
              is all concerned with the topic of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#UniversalConstructions"} below
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %h3#CategoriesAndFunctors Categories and Functors
            %p
              The notion of a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
              below) embodies the idea of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structuralism"} structuralism
              applied to concepts in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              (or generally:
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              that belong to it, also all the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"}> structure
                \-preserving maps
              between them, hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              in the case of
              = succeed "-style" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bourbaki"} Bourbaki
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structures"} mathematical structures
            %p
              The first achievement of the notion of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              is to abstract away from such manifestly
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
              (Examples
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfConcreteCategories"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StructuredSetsAndFaithfulFunctors"}
              below) to more indirectly defined mathematical objects whose “structure” is only defined, after the fact, by which maps, now just called
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %p
              This
              = succeed "-principle" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structuralism"} structuralism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              themselves to be those “maps” that respect their
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structuralism"} structuralism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              between their objects: These are the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Functors"}
              below).
            %p
              For the purpose of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              are the assignments of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
                  to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpacesViaAlgebrasOfFunctions"}
              below.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            #Categories.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"}> category
                  )
              %p
                A
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                is
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Obj
                              %mi 𝒞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %em
                        class of
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                %li
                  %p
                    for each
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Obj
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                    of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,Y)
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+of+morphisms"} set of morphisms
                        from
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                        to
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi Y
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  %p We denote the elements of this set by arrows like this:
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi f
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} Y \;\;\in Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,Y)
                          \\,.
                %li
                  %p
                    for each
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Obj
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                    a morphism
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi X
                          %mi X
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \overset{id_X}{\to} X \;\; \in Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,X)
                  %p
                    called the
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
                    on
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %li
                  %p
                    for each
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple"} triple
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Obj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1, X_2, X_3 \in Obj
                    of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mtd
                                  %mo ×
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 3
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mo ∘
                                        %mrow
                                          %msub
                                            %mi X
                                            %mn 1
                                          %mo ,
                                          %msub
                                            %mi X
                                            %mn 2
                                          %mo ,
                                          %msub
                                            %mi X
                                            %mn 3
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 3
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                                %mtd
                                  %mo ,
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 3
                                %mtd
                                  %mo ↦
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi g
                                      %mo ∘
                                      %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\array{
                          Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X_1, X_2)
                          \&amp;\times&amp;
                          Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X_2, X_3)
                          \&amp;\overset{\circ_{X_1,X_2,X_3}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                          Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X_1, X_3)
                          \\\
                          X_1 \overset{f}{\to} X_2
                          \&amp;,&amp;
                          X_2 \overset{f}{\to} X_3
                          \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                          X_1 \overset{ g \circ f }{\longrightarrow} X_3
                          }
                  %p
                    called
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              %p such that:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    for all
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Obj
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unitality
                    holds: given
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \overset{f}{\to} Y \;\;\in Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,Y)
                  %p then
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi Y
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi f
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi f
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ∘
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi X
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ;
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \overset{id_Y \circ f}{\longrightarrow} Y
                          \\;=\;
                          X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} Y
                          \\;=\;
                          X \overset{f \circ id_X }{\longrightarrow} Y
                          \\,;
                %li
                  %p
                    for all
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadruples"} quadruples
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 4
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Obj
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1, X_2, X_3, X_4 \in Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                    satifies
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 12
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 23
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 3
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 34
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X_1
                          \\overset{f_{12}}{\to}
                          X_2
                          \\overset{f_{23}}{\to}
                          X_3
                          \\overset{f_{34}}{\to}
                          X_4
                  %p then
                  .maruku-equation
