                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ_{X_1,X_2,X_3} = \text{ordinary composition of functions}
                    \.
            %p
              More generally all kind of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  sets with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bourbaki"} Bourbaki
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              are the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              (whence the name “morphism”!). These are called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
              (we characterize them precisely in Example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StructuredSetsAndFaithfulFunctors"}
            #ExamplesOfConcreteCategories.num_example
