            %h3#NaturalTransformationsAndPresheaves Natural transformations and presheaves
            %p
              Given a system of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"}> homo-
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              (“transformations”) in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_X \overset{\phantom{A}\eta_X\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow} G_X
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              that depend on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Functors"}
              = succeed "," do
                %em natural
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NaturalTransformations"}
              below) if it is compatible with (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"}> homo-
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of the variable itself.
            %p
              These
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              are the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mi η
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \overset{\phantom{A}\eta\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow} G
                    \\,,
            %p
              and hence there is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+functors"} category of functors
              between any two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              (Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorCategory"}
              below).
            %p
              A key class of such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+categories"} functor categories
              are those between an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}
              and the base
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
              (Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfPresheaves"}
              below). It makes good sense (Remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresaheavesAsGeneralizedSpaces"}
              below) to think of these as categories of “generalized objects of
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaLemma"}
              below) and the resulting
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaEmbedding"}
              below). This innocent-looking lemma is the heart that makes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              tick.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            #NaturalTransformations.num_defn
              %h6#definition_10 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %p
                Given two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
