                Now the defining property of epimorphisms (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Monomorphism"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %mi im
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi η
                            %mi X
                            %mo ♯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ♯
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi iso
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi mono
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mono
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\eta^{\sharp}_{ im(\eta^\sharp_X) }
                      \\;=\;
                      iso \circ mono
                      \\;=\;
                      mono.
              %p
                This shows that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi conc
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi im
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                        %mo ♯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} conc X \coloneqq im(\eta^\sharp_X)
                is indeed concret.
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
              %p
                It remains to show that this construction is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                to the inclusion. We claim that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctionUnitFromHomIsomorphism"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi conc
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi conc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (conc \dashv \iota_{conc})
                is provided by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi η
                        %mi conc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{conc}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConcretificationUnitFromEpiMonoFactorization"} (89)
              %p
                To see this, first notice that, since the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2C+mono%29+factorization+system"} epi/mono-factorization
                (Prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheafToposEpiMonoFactorization"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal
                and hence
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagrams"} commuting diagrams
                of the form
              #eq:NaturalitySquareForConcretificationUnit.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (91)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %munderover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi epi
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi X
                                        %mn 1
                                    %mi conc
                            %mtd
                              %mi im
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi η
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ♯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi mono
                            %mtd
                              %mo ♯
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %munderover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi epi
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi X
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mi conc
                            %mtd
                              %mi im
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi η
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ♯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi mono
                            %mtd
                              %mo ♯
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X_1
                      \&amp;\underoverset{epi}{\eta^{conc}_{X_1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      im(\eta^\sharp_{X_1})
                      \&amp;\underset{mono}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      \\sharp X_1
                      \\\
                      \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                      \\\
                      X_2
                      \&amp;\underoverset{epi}{\eta^{conc}_{X_2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      im(\eta^\sharp_{X_2})
                      \&amp;\underset{mono}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      \\sharp X_2
                      }
              %p
                Now to demonstrate the adjunction it is sufficient, by Prop.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi η
                        %mi conc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{conc}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphism"} universal morphism
                in the sense of Def.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalArrow"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X_1 \to X_2
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mi conc
                        %mo ↪
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
