                      \\end{aligned}
            %p (…)
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %div
            %h2#BasicNotionsOfHomotopyTheory Basic notions of homotopy theory
            %p
              Traditionally,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              have been
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} founded
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              is that of “bags of distinguishable points”.
            %p
              But fundamental
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              is governed by the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+principle"} gauge principle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+history"} field histories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
              or not, instead one has to ask where there is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi γ
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \stackrel{\gamma}{\longrightarrow} y
            %p
              between them. In mathematics this is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %p
              This principle applies also to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
              themselves, and thus leads to
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-of-gauge+transformations"} gauge-of-gauge transformations
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies+of+homotopies"} homotopies of homotopies
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/2Cell.jpg", :width => "200"}/
            %p
              and so on to ever
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
              or
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopies"} higher homotopies
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/3Cell.jpg", :width => "200"}/
            %p
              This shows that what
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              here are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              of is not really a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              in the sense of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              with
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopies"} higher homotopies
              between them is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %p
              Hence the theory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              –
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              – is much like
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              built right into its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are simply
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paths"} paths
              between points represent the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} equivalent
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              viewed, in turn, up to “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"}> weak homotopy equivalence
              ”.
            %p
              In the special case of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              with a single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
              necessarily go from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              to itself and hence form a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetries"} symmetries
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/GroupActing.jpg", :width => "80"}/
            %p
              This way
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              subsumes
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            %p
              If there are higher order
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-of-gauge+transformations"} gauge-of-gauge transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies+of+homotopies"} homotopies of homotopies
              between these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
              = succeed "-elements," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groups"} 3-groups
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groups"} n-groups
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are represented by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
              are represented by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            %p
              This way
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              subsumes parts of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            %p
              Since, generally, there is more than one element in a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Groupoid"}
            %p
              If there are higher order
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge-of-gauge+transformations"} gauge-of-gauge transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies+of+homotopies"} homotopies of homotopies
              between the transformations in such a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoids"} 2-groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groupoids"} 3-groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoids"} n-groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              are recovered as the special case of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-groupoids"} 0-groupoids
            %p
              Due to the higher orders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              appearing here,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structures"} mathematical structures
              based not on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              but on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are also called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Structures"} higher structures
            %p
              Hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are equivalently
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              are the unification of plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              with the concept of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %p
              An efficient way of handling
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              is in their explicit guise as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanComplexe"}
              below); these are the non-abelian generalization of the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              used in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homotopy"} chain homotopy
              is a special case of the general concept of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
              forms but a special abelian corner within
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              may be understood as the non-abelian generalization of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            %p
              Hence, in a self-reflective manner, there are many different but
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent
              incarnations of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#TopologicalHomotopyTheory"} Topological homotopy theory
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
                  modeled by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  familiar from traditional
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
                  = succeed "-theory." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              %li
                %p
                  %em>
                    %a{:href => "#SimplicialHomotopyTheory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                  \.
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
                  modeled on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
                  are the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
                  to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
                  (the “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"}> homotopy hypothesis
                  ”), which makes explicit that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  is not really about
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
                  that these represent.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Ideally, abstract homotopy theory would simply be a complete replacement of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
              %em removing
              the assumption of strict
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalence"} gauge equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
              themselves, not requiring any further discussion. This ideal perspective is the promise of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
              and may become full practical reality in the next decades.
            %p
              Until then, abstract homotopy theory has to be formulated on top of the traditional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
              provided by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %p
              A very convenient and powerful such emulator for homotopy theory within set theory is
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model category theory
              %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"} Quillen 67
              and highly developed since. This we introduce here.
            %p
              The idea is to consider ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X
                    \\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}
                    Y
            %p
              should be
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalence"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Isomorphism"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
              defining an actual isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^{-1} \circ f \;=\; id_{X}
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    f \circ f^{-1} \;=\; id_Y
            %p
              but intended to satisfy this only with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
              relaxed to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            #eq:HomotopyEquivalenceCondition.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (92)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi gauge
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi gauge
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^{-1} \circ f \;\overset{gauge}{\Rightarrow}\; id_{X}
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    f \circ f^{-1} \;\overset{gauge}{\Rightarrow}\; id_Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              Such
              %em would-be homotopy equivalences
              are called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
              below).
            %p
              In principle, this information already defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              by a construction called
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              into actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
              in a suitable way.
            %p
              However, without further tools this construction is unwieldy. The extra structure of a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              below) on top of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              provides a set of tools.
            %p
              The idea here is to abstract (in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightHomotopyInAModelCategory"}
              below) from the evident concepts in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
              of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+homotopy"} right homotopy
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RightHomotopy"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyl(X)  = X \times [0,1]
              or into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Path
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Path(X) = X^{[0,1]}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
              serves to parameterize the relevant
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %p
              Now a little reflection shows (this was the seminal insight of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"} Quillen 67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
              factors the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+morphism"} diagonal morphism
              from a space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi diag
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mtext weak equiv.
                      %mtext cofibration
                    %mi Path
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mtext fibration
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    diag_X
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X
                    \\underoverset{\text{weak equiv.}}{\text{ cofibration }}{\longrightarrow}
                    Path(X)
                    \\overset{\text{ fibration }}{\longrightarrow}
                    X \times X
            %p
              while the cylinder serves to factor the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal+morphism"} codiagonal morphism
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi codiag
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mtext cofibration
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mtext weak equiv
                      %mtext fibration
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    codiag_X
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X \sqcup X
                    \\overset{ \text{cofibration} }{\longrightarrow}
                    Cyl(X)
                    \\underoverset{ \text{weak equiv} }{ \text{fibration} }{\longrightarrow}
                    X
            %p
              where in both cases “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"}> fibration
              ” means something like
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  well behaved
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  satisfying the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                  (Def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingAndExtension"}
                  below) against fibrations that are also weak equivalences
            %p
              Such factorizations subject to lifting properties is what the definition of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              axiomatizes, in some generality. That this indeed provides a good toolbox for handling
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
              is shown by the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              (Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WhiteheadTheoremInModelCategories"}
              below), which exhibits all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              as actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
              after passage to “good representatives” of objects (fibrant/cofibrant
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolutions"} resolutions
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              below). Accordingly, the first theorem of model category theory (
              %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, I.1 theorem 1
              , reproduced as Theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              below), provides a tractable expression for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              modulo
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              of the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              in terms of actual morphisms out of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolutions"} cofibrant resolutions
              into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+resolutions"} fibrant resolutions
              (Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomsOutOfCofibrantIntoFibrantComputeHomotopyCategory"}
              below).
            %p
              This is then generally how
              = succeed "-theory" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+homotopy+fiber+sequences"} long homotopy fiber sequences
              (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LongFiberSequence"}
              below), are reflected via constructions of ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              but applied to suitably
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolved objects
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              %strong Literature
              (
              %a{:href => "model+category#DwyerSpalinski95"}> Dwyer-Spalinski 95
              )
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            #ModelCategory.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"}> model category
                  )
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                is
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    (Def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                    (Def.
                    = succeed ");" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Limits"}
                %li
                  %p
                    three sub-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Fib
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Cof
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Mor
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W, Fib, Cof \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
                    of its class of
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %p such that
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the class
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                    makes
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    into a
                    = succeed "," do
                      %strong
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
                %li
                  %p
                    The pairs
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Cof
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Fib
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \cap Cof\;,\; Fib)
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Cap
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Fib
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Cap\;,\; W\cap Fib)
                    are both
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
              %p One says:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    elements in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                    are
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                %li
                  %p
                    elements in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cof
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof
                    are
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    elements in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Fib
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib
                    are
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    elements in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Cof
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W\cap Cof
                    are
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    elements in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Fib
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Fib
                    are
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
            %p
              The form of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              is due to (
              %a{:href => "model+category#Joyal"}> Joyal, def. E.1.2
              ). It implies various other conditions that (
              %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67
              ) demands explicitly, see prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakEquivalencesAreClosedUnderRetracts"}
              below.
            %p
              We now dicuss the concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
              below) appearing in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
            %h3#WeakFactorizationSystems Factorization systems
            #LiftingAndExtension.num_defn
              %h6#definition_2 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                be any
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p}}\downarrow
                      \\\
                      B
                      }
              %p
                then an
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                along the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is a completion to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↗
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p}}\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\tilde f}}
                      \\\
                      B
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                Dually, given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; A
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                      \\\
                      X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                      }
              %p
                then a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                through
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is a completion to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; A
                      \\\
                      \&amp;{}^{\mathllap{\tilde f}}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                      \\\
                      X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                Combining these cases: given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi l
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi r
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X_1 &amp;\stackrel{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_1
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p_l}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_r}}
                      \\\
                      X_2 &amp;\stackrel{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_2
                      }
              %p
                then a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting"} lifting
                in the diagram is a completion to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi l
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi r
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X_1 &amp;\stackrel{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_1
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p_l}}\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_r}}
                      \\\
                      X_2 &amp;\stackrel{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_2
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                Given a sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                of morphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
              %ul
                %li
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_r
                  as above is said to have the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                    against
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  or to be a
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
                  if in all square diagrams with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_r
                  on the right and any
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi l
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_l \in K
                  on the left a lift exists.
              %p dually:
              %ul
                %li
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi l
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_l
                  is said to have the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                    against
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  or to be a
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+morphism"} projective morphism
                  if in all square diagrams with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi l
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_l
                  on the left and any
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi r
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_r \in K
                  on the left a lift exists.
            #WeakFactorizationSystem.num_defn
              %h6#definition_3 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"}> weak factorization systems
                  )
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
                (WFS) on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Proj
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Proj,Inj)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                such that
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    Every
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X\to Y
                    of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    may be factored as the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                    of a morphism in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Proj
                    followed by one in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Inj
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Proj
                          %mi Z
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Inj
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          f\;\colon\;  X \overset{\in Proj}{\longrightarrow} Z \overset{\in Inj}{\longrightarrow} Y
                          \\,.
                %li
                  %p
                    The classes are closed under having the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingAndExtension"}
                  %ol
                    %li
                      %p
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi Proj
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Proj
                        is precisely the class of morphisms having the
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                        against every morphisms in
                        = succeed ";" do
                          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                            %semantics
                              %mrow
                                %mi Inj
                              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Inj
                    %li
                      %p
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi Inj
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Inj
                        is precisely the class of morphisms having the
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                        against every morphisms in
                        = succeed "." do
                          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                            %semantics
                              %mrow
                                %mi Proj
                              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Proj
            #FunctorialFactorization.num_defn
              %h6#definition_4 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"}> functorial factorization
                  )
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
                of the morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi fact
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      fact \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}
              %p
                which is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1 \;\colon \;\mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}\to \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark Remark
              %p
                In def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorialFactorization"}
                we are using the following standard notation, see at
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
                and at
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+of+a+category"} nerve of a category
              %p
                Write
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [1] = \{0 \to 1\}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [2] = \{0 \to 1 \to 2\}
                for the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+numbers"} ordinal numbers
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
                and hence as
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Arr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(\mathcal{C})
                is equivalently the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi Funct
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]} \coloneqq Funct(\Delta[1], \mathcal{C})
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}\coloneqq Funct(\Delta[2], \mathcal{C})
                has as objects pairs of composable morphisms in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i \colon [1] \rightarrow [2]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i
                omits the index
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                in its image. By precomposition, this induces
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i  \colon \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1
                    sends a pair of composable morphisms to their
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_2
                    sends a pair of composable morphisms to the first morphisms;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0
                    sends a pair of composable morphisms to the second morphisms.
            #FunctorialWeakFactorizationSystem.num_defn
              %h6#definition_5 Definition
              %p
                A
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
                %strong functorial weak factorization system
                if the factorization of morphisms may be chosen to be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi fact
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fact
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorialFactorization"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi fact
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_2 \circ fact
                lands in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Proj
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi fact
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0\circ fact
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Inj
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_2 Remark
              %p
                Not all weak factorization systems are functorial, def.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorialWeakFactorizationSystem"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
                (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallObjectArgument"}
                below), with due care) are.
            #ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                and let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+morphisms"} projective morphisms
                and of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingAndExtension"}
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    Both classes contain the class of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    of
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %li
                  %p
                    Both classes are closed under
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                    in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                    is also closed under
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
                %li
                  %p
                    Both classes are closed under forming
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
                    (see remark
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfMorphisms"}
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                    is closed under forming
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
                    of morphisms in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    (“
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobase+change"}> cobase change
                    ”).
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mi Inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
                    is closed under forming
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                    of morphisms in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    (“
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"}> base change
                    ”).
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                    is closed under forming
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                    in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mi Inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
                    is closed under forming
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                    in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p We go through each item in turn.
              %p
                %strong containing isomorphisms
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi Iso
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi g
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      A &amp;\overset{f}{\rightarrow}&amp; X
                      \\\
                      {}_{\mathllap{\in Iso}}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                      \\\
                      B &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                      }
              %p
                with the left morphism an isomorphism, then a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                is given by using the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
                of this isomorphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %mo ↗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{{f \circ i^{-1}}}\nearrow
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in K
                and so
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K Proj
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %p
                %strong closure under composition
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                    %mi Inj
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                    %mi Inj
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in K}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                      \\\
                      B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                      }
              %p
                consider its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
                decomposition as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                    %mi Inj
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi K
                                    %mi Inj
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
