              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1}
              grow larger and larger.
            %p
              The concept of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              is just what makes this intuition precise and finishes the small object argument. For the present purpose we just need the following simple version:
            #ClassOfMorphismsWithSmallDomains.num_defn
              %h6#definition_6 Definition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
                a sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of its morphisms, say that these have
                %em
                  small
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
                if there is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
