            %p
              We now spell out that def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              indeed satisfies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              at its weak equivalences.
            #WhiteheadTheoremInModelCategories.num_lemma
              %h6#lemma_5 Lemma
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
                  in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                be a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                between two objects which are both
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomotopyEquivalenceCondition"} (92)
            .proof
              %h6#proof_9 Proof
              %p
                By the factorization axioms in the model category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                and by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \longrightarrow Y
                factors through an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                as an acyclic cofibration followed by an acyclic fibration. In particular it follows that with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                both fibrant and cofibrant, so is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              %p
                So let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
