                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}_{f c}, W_{f c})
            #CategoriesOfFibrantObjects.num_remark
              %h6#remark_6 Remark
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+fibrant+objects"} categories of fibrant objects
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration+categories"} cofibration categories
              %p
                Of course the subcategories in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
                inherit more structure than just that of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
                from
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_c
                each inherit “half” of the factorization axioms. One says that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
                has the structure of a “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+category"}> fibration category
                ” called a “Brown-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"}> category of fibrant objects
                ”, while
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_c
                has the structure of a “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration+category"}> cofibration category
                ”.
              %p
                We discuss properties of these categories of (co-)fibrant objects below in
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#HomotopyFiberSequences"} Homotopy fiber sequences
            %p
              The proof of theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              immediately implies the following:
            #HomotopyCategoryOfSubcategoriesOfModelCategoriesOnGoodObjects.num_cor
              %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow Ho(\mathcal{C})
                from def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
                (using remark
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EssentialUniquenessOfLocalizationFunctorOfModelCategory"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
                of def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
