            %p
              The key fact that makes def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}
              practically relevant is the following:
            #KenBrownLemma.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"}> Ken Brown's lemma
                  )
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f, \mathcal{C}_c
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} of fibrant objects
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration+category"} of cofibrant objects
                respectively (def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                be a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    A
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                    out of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mi f
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}_f \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
                  %p
                    is a
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+functor"} homotopical functor
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopicalFunctor"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
                    to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                %li
                  %p
                    A
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                    out of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mi c
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}_c \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
                  %p
                    is a
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+functor"} homotopical functor
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopicalFunctor"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                    to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            %p
              The following proof refers to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FactorizationLemma"}
            .proof
              %h6#proof_14 Proof
              %p
                We discuss the case of a functor on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                be a weak equivalence in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Path
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Path(X)
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathAndCylinderObjectsInAModelCategory"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Path
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi Fib
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi pb
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi f
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Path
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                    %mo ∩
                                    %mi Fib
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                    %mo ∩
                                    %mi Fib
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Path(f) &amp;\underset{\in W \cap Fib}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p_1^\ast f}}_{\mathllap{\in W}}\downarrow
                      \&amp;(pb)&amp;
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in W}}
                      \\\
                      Path(Y) &amp;\overset{p_1}{\underset{\in W \cap Fib}{\longrightarrow}}&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{p_0}}_{\mathllap{\in W \cap Fib}}\downarrow
                      \\\
                      Y
                      }
                      \\,,
              %p
                where the square is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Path
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Path(f)
                on the top left is our notation for the universal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                object. (Below we discuss this in more detail, it is the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cocone"} mapping cocone
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingConeAndMappingCocone"}
              %p Here:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
                    are both acyclic fibrations, by lemma
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentMapsOfCylinderAndPathSpaceInGoodSituation"}
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Path
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Path(f) \to X
                    is an acyclic fibration because it is the pullback of
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1^\ast f
                    is a weak equivalence, because the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FactorizationLemma"}
                    states that the composite vertical morphism factors
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    through a weak equivalence, hence if
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    is a weak equivalence, then
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1^\ast f
                    is by
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
                    (def.
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
              %p
                Now apply the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                to this diagram and use the assumption that it sends acyclic fibrations to weak equivalences to obtain
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Path
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Path
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi W
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      F(Path(f)) &amp;\underset{\in W }{\longrightarrow}&amp; F(X)
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{F(p_1^\ast f)}}_{\mathllap{}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F(f)}}
                      \\\
                      F(Path(Y)) &amp;\overset{F(p_1)}{\underset{\in W }{\longrightarrow}}&amp; F(Y)
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{F(p_0)}}_{\mathllap{\in W}}\downarrow
                      \\\
                      Y
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                But the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FactorizationLemma"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ∘
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_0 \circ p_1^\ast f
                is a fibration, hence an acyclic fibration by the above. Therefore also
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ∘
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(p_0 \circ p_1^\ast f)
                is a weak equivalence. Now the claim that also
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(f)
                is a weak equivalence follows with applying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
            #LeftAndRightDerivedFunctors.num_cor
              %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}
                be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
                and consider
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C}\longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
                a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    If
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    preserves cofibrant objects and acyclic cofibrations between these, then its
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
                    (def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕃
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}F
                    exists, fitting into a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                    %mi c
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi 𝒟
                                    %mi c
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⇙
                                    %mo ≃
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mi 𝒟
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi 𝕃
                                      %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒟
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\array{
                          \\mathcal{C}_{c} &amp;\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathcal{D}_{c}
                          \\\
                          {}^{\mathllap{\gamma_{\mathcal{C}}}}\downarrow
                          \&amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                          \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\gamma_{\mathcal{D}}}}
                          \\\
                          Ho(\mathcal{C}) &amp;\overset{\mathbb{L}F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Ho(\mathcal{D})
                          }
                %li
                  %p
                    If
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    preserves fibrant objects and acyclic fibrants between these, then its
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+derived+functor"} right derived functor
                    (def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}F
                    exists, fitting into a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                    %mi f
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi 𝒟
                                    %mi f
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⇙
                                    %mo ≃
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mi 𝒟
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mtd
                                  %munder
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi ℝ
                                      %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒟
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\array{
                          \\mathcal{C}_{f} &amp;\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathcal{D}_{f}
                          \\\
                          {}^{\mathllap{\gamma_{\mathcal{C}}}}\downarrow
                          \&amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                          \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\gamma_{\mathcal{D}}}}
                          \\\
                          Ho(\mathcal{C}) &amp;\underset{\mathbb{R}F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Ho(\mathcal{D})
                          }
                          \\,.
            #ComputationOfLeftRightDerivedFunctorsViaResolutions.num_example
              %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (construction of left/right
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
                be a functor between two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
                (def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    If
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    preserves fibrant objects and weak equivalences between fibrant objects, then the total
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+derived+functor"} right derived functor
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi F
                          %mo ≔
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi γ
                            %mi 𝒟
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}F \coloneqq \mathbb{R}(\gamma_{\mathcal{D}}\circ F)
                    (def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                    %mi f
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %mi 𝒟
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mrow
                                            %msub
                                              %mi 𝒞
                                              %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⇙
                                    %mo ≃
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mi 𝒟
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mtd
                                  %munder
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi ℝ
                                      %mi F
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Ho
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi 𝒟
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\array{
                          \\mathcal{C}_f &amp;\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathcal{D}
                          \\\
                          {}^{\mathllap{\gamma_{\mathcal{C}_f}}}\downarrow
                          \&amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                          \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\gamma_{\mathcal{D}}}}
                          \\\
                          Ho(\mathcal{C})
                          \&amp;\underset{\mathbb{R}F}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                          Ho(\mathcal{D})
                          }
                  %p
                    is given, up to isomorphism, on any object
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi 𝒞
                          %mi Ho
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in \mathcal{C} \overset{\gamma_{\mathcal{C}}}{\longrightarrow} Ho(\mathcal{C})
                    by appying
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    to a fibrant replacement
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
                    of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    and then forming a cofibrant replacement
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi P
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(F(P X))
                    of the result:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}F(X)
                      \\simeq
                      Q(F(P X))
                      \\,.
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    If
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    preserves cofibrant objects and weak equivalences between cofibrant objects, then the total
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕃
                          %mi F
