              the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              of the adjoint pair.
            %p
              The archetypical example of a pair of adjoint functors is that consisting of forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times (-)
              and forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon L(d) \to c
              is any morphism, then the image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{d,c}(f) \colon d \to R(c)
              is called its
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi f
                        %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{
                    L(c) \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} d
                    }{
                    c \overset{\tilde f}{\longrightarrow} R(d)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              For an object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in \mathcal{D}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L d
              is called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi d
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                      %mi L
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_d \;\colon\; d \longrightarrow R L d
            %p
              For an object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R c
              is called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi c
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi L
                      %mi R
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_c \;\colon\; L R c \longrightarrow c
            %p
              Adjunction units and counits turn out to encode the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
              of all other morphisms by the formulas
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi η
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mi d
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                            %mi f
                        %mi R
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{(L d\overset{f}{\to}c)} = (d\overset{\eta}{\to} R L d \overset{R f}{\to} R c)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                            %mi R
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mi d
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                            %mi g
                        %mi L
                        %mi R
                        %mi c
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi ϵ
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{(d\overset{g}{\to} R c)} = (L d \overset{L g}{\to} L R c \overset{\epsilon}{\to} c)
                  \.
            #QuillenAdjunction.num_defn
              %h6#definition_16 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"}> Quillen adjunction
                  )
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}
                be
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfNaturalBijectionOfHomSets"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi R
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi L
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (L \dashv R)
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\mathcal{C}
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                      {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {}
                      \\mathcal{D}
              %p
                is called a
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi Qu
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊥
                            %mi Qu
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi R
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi L
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{C}
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                      {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {{}_{\phantom{Qu}}\bot_{Qu}}
                      \\mathcal{D}
              %p
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                are called left/right
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quillen functors
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                    preserves
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                    preserves
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                    preserves
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                    preserves
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                    preserves
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                    and
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                    preserves
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
            #ConditionsOnQuillenAdjunctionAreIndeedEquivalent.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
              %p
                The conditions in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunction"}
                are indeed all equivalent.
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, I.4, theorem 3
              )
            .proof
              %h6#proof_16 Proof
              %p First observe that
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    (i)
                    %em
                      A
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                      between
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
                      preserves acyclic cofibrations precisely if its
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                      preserves fibrations.
                %li
                  %p
                    (ii)
                    %em
                      A
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                      between
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
                      preserves cofibrations precisely if its
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                      preserves acyclic fibrations.
              %p
                We discuss statement (i), statement (ii) is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
                be an acyclic cofibration in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon X \to Y
                a fibration in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                as on the left of the following, its
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L\dashv R)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                is a commuting diagram as on the right here:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi R
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi L
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi g
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; R(X)
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{R(g)}}
                      \\\
                      B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; R(Y)
                      }
                      \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                      \\,,
                      \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                      \\array{
                      L(A) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{L(f)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                      \\\
                      L(B) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                preserves acyclic cofibrations, then the diagram on the right has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L\dashv R)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                of that lift is a lift of the left diagram. This shows that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(g)
                has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against all acylic cofibrations and hence is a fibration. Conversely, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                preserves fibrations, the same argument run from right to left gives that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                preserves acyclic fibrations.
              %p Now by repeatedly applying (i) and (ii), all four conditions in question are seen to be equivalent.
            %p
              The following is the analog of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
