              %p given by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Cyl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi R
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\tilde \eta \;\colon\; Cyl(X) \longrightarrow R X
                      \\,.
              %p
                This establishes the adjunction. Now regarding the (co-)units: We show this for the adjunction unit, the case of the adjunction counit is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formally dual
              %p
                First observe that for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒟
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}_c
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
                from def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
