              %p
                Accordingly the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
                of a topological space is the result of shrinking both ends of the cylinder on the object two the point. This is homeomoprhic to attaching two copies of the cone on the space at the base of the cone.
              %p
                (graphics taken from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://personal.us.es/fmuro/files/slides/praha.pdf"} Muro 2010
              %p
                Below in example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardTopologicalMappingConeIsHomotopyCofiber"}
                we find the homotopy-theoretic interpretation of this standard topological mapping cone as a model for the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
            #UnreducedCone.num_remark
              %h6#remark_9 Remark
              %p
                The
                %em formula
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
                in prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConeAndMappingCylinder"}
                (as opposed to that of the mapping co-cone) does not require the presence of the basepoint: for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                a morphism in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                (as opposed to in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Y
                      %munder
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi X
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Cone'(f) \coloneqq Y \underset{X}{\sqcup} Cone'(X)
                      \\,,
              %p
                where the prime denotes the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em unreduced cone
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            #UnreducedMappingConeAsReducedConeOfBasedPointAdjoined.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_17 Proposition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                a morphism in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnreducedCone"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times I
                def.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalInterval"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingConeAndMappingCocone"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo +
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_+ \colon X_+ \to Y_+
                (with a basepoint adjoined, def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasePointAdjoined"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cylinder"} reduced cylinder
                (example
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardReducedCyclinderInTop"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Cone'(f) \simeq Cone(f_+)
                      \\,.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_26 Proof
              %p
                By prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitsAndColimitsOfPointedObjects"}
                and example
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeAndSmashOfBasePointAdjoinedTopologicalSpaces"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(f_+)
                is given by the colimit in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                over the following diagram:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ×
                              %mi I
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Cone
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \sqcup \ast &amp;\overset{(f,id)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y \sqcup \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      X \sqcup\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (X \times I) \sqcup \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Cone(f_+)
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p We may factor the vertical maps to give
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ×
                              %mi I
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Cone
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo +
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Cone
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \sqcup \ast &amp;\overset{(f,id)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y \sqcup \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      X \sqcup\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (X \times I) \sqcup \ast
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \\ast \sqcup \ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Cone'(f)_+
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Cone'(f)
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                This way the top part of the diagram (using the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                to compute the colimit in two stages) is manifestly a cocone under the result of applying
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_+
                to the diagram for the unreduced cone. Since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_+
                is itself given by a colimit, it preserves colimits, and hence gives the partial colimit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone'(f)_+
                as shown. The remaining pushout then contracts the remaining copy of the point away.
            %p
              Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingConesInTopologicalSpaces"}
              makes it clear that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              that happens to be in the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              can be
              %em continuously
              translated in the cylinder-direction, keeping it constant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyGroupsOftopologicalSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              vanishes in the mapping cone. Hence in the mapping cone
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  the image of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is removed up to homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(f)
              is a homotopy-version of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            #FactorizationLemma.num_lemma
              %h6#lemma_11 Lemma
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"}> factorization lemma
                  )
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_c
                be a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                the
                = succeed "-construction" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConeAndMappingCylinder"}
                provides a cofibration resolution of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the composite morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %mi Cyl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %mi f
                          %mi Cyl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{i_0}{\longrightarrow} Cyl(X) \overset{(i_1)_\ast f}{\longrightarrow} Cyl(f)
                    is a cofibration;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    factors through this morphism by a weak equivalence left inverse to an acyclic cofibration
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Cof
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %mi f
                              %mo ∘
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %mi Cyl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi W
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          f
                          \\;\colon\;
                          X
                          \\underoverset{\in Cof}{(i_1)_\ast f\circ i_0}{\longrightarrow}
                          Cyl(f)
                          \\underset{\in W}{\longrightarrow}
                          Y
                          \\,,
              %p Dually:
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
                be a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                the
                = succeed "-construction" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cocylinder"} mapping cocylinder
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConeAndMappingCylinder"}
                provides a fibration resolution of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the composite morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Path
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi p
                                %mn 1
                                %mo *
                              %mi f
                          %mi Path
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
