              %p
                Moreover, the pairing operation induced on the objects in the image of this functor via remark
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConcatenatedLoopSpaceObject"}
                (concatenation of loops) gives the objects in the image of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                structure, and makes this functor lift as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
