            .proof
              %h6#proof_42 Proof
              %p
                That there are long sequences of this form is the result of combining prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFiberOfHomotopyFiberIsLooping"}
                and prop.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExactSequenceOfHomotopyFiberAtOneStage"}
              %p
                It only remains to see that it is indeed the morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\Omega} f
                that appear, as indicated.
              %p
                In order to see this, it is convenient to adopt the following notation: for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                a morphism, then we denote the collection of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
                of its homotopy fiber as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇝
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      hofib(f)
                      \=
                      \\left\{
                      (x, f(x) \overset{\gamma_1}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast)
                      \\right\}
              %p
                indicating that these elements are pairs consisting of an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and a “path” (an element of the given path space object) from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
                to the basepoint.
              %p
                This way the canonical map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(f) \to X
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇝
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, f(x) \rightsquigarrow \ast) \mapsto x
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇝
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇝
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 2
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      hofib(hofib(f))
                      \=
                      \\left\{
                      ( (x, f(x) \overset{\gamma_1}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast),
                      x \overset{\gamma_2}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast  )
                      \\right\}
                      \\,.
              %p
                This identifies with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega Y
                by forming the loops
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi γ
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\gamma_1 \cdot f(\overline{\gamma_2})
                      \\,,
              %p where the overline denotes reversal and the dot denotes concatenation.
              %p Then consider the next homotopy fiber
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo ⇝
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 1
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mover
                            %mo ⇝
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 2
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi x
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mover
                                      %mo ⇝
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mn 3
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo *
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mover
                                      %mo ⇝
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi f
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                        %msub
                                          %mi γ
                                          %mn 3
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo *
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %msub
                                      %mrow
                                      %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                        %mrow
                                          %msub
                                            %mi γ
                                            %mn 1
                                    %mo ↘
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo ⇒
                                  %mtd
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ↙
                                      %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                        %mrow
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                  %mtd
                                    %mo *
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      hofib(hofib(hofib(f)))
                      \=
                      \\left\{
                      \\left(
                      ( (x, f(x) \overset{\gamma_1}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast), x \overset{\gamma_2}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast  ),
                      \\left(
                      \\array{
                      x &amp;&amp; \overset{\gamma_3}{\rightsquigarrow} &amp;&amp; \ast
                      \\\
                      f(x) &amp;&amp;\overset{f(\gamma_3)}{\rightsquigarrow}&amp;&amp; \ast
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\gamma_1}}\searrow &amp; \Rightarrow &amp; \swarrow_{\mathllap{}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \ast
                      }
                      \\right)
                      \\right)
                      \\right\}
                      \\,,
              %p
                where on the right we have a path in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(f)
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⇝
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi γ
                            %mn 1
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, f(x)\overset{\gamma_1}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast)
                to the basepoint element. This is a path
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_3
                together with a path-of-paths which connects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\gamma_3)
              %p
                By the above convention this is identified with the loop in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                which is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\gamma_2 \cdot (\overline{\gamma}_3)
                      \\,.
              %p
                But the map to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(hofib(f))
                sends this data to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇝
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 1
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mover
                          %mo ⇝
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mn 2
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( (x, f(x) \overset{\gamma_1}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast), x \overset{\gamma_2}{\rightsquigarrow} \ast  )
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 3
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 3
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo ⋅
                                  %msub
                                    %mover
                                      %mi γ
                                      %mo ¯
                                    %mn 3
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo ⋅
                                  %msub
                                    %mover
                                      %mi γ
                                      %mo ¯
                                    %mn 3
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ¯
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      \\gamma_1 \cdot f( \overline{\gamma_2} )
                      \&amp; \simeq
                      f(\gamma_3) \cdot f(\overline{\gamma_2})
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      f( \gamma_3 \cdot \overline{\gamma_2} )
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      f ( \overline{\gamma_2 \cdot \overline{\gamma}_3} )
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\overline{f(\gamma_2 \cdot \overline{\gamma}_3) }
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,,
              %p
                hence to the reveral of the image under
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                of the loop in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_14 Remark
              %p
                In (
                %a{:href => "model+category#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, I.3, prop. 3, prop. 4
                ) more is shown than stated in prop.
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LongFiberSequence"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega  Y \to hofib(f)
                is not just shown to exist, but is described in detail via an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega Y
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(f)
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(\mathcal{C})
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi hofib
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi hofib
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega Y \simeq hofib(hofib(f))
            #LongExactSequeceOfHomotopyGroups.num_example
              %h6#example_10 Example
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"}> compactly generated
                ) from theorem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mo +
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(I_+,X)
                from def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalPathSpace"}
                and example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedMappingSpace"}
                as the abstract path space objects in def.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathAndCylinderObjectsInAModelCategory"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalPathSpaceIsGoodPathSpaceObject"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi n
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [\ast, \Omega^n X] \simeq \pi_n(X)
              %p
                is the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyGroupsOftopologicalSpaces"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                at its basepoint.
              %p
                Hence using
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
