                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalHomotopyEquivalencesAreWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
                is not true generally: not every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                between topological spaces is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              %p However, as we will discuss below, it turns out that
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    every weak homotopy equivalence between
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
                    is a homotopy equivalence (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead%27s+theorem"}> Whitehead's theorem
                    , cor.
                    = succeed ");" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WhiteheadTheorem"}
                %li
                  %p
                    every topological space is connected by a weak homotopy equivalence to a CW-complex (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+approximation"}> CW approximation
                    , remark
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EveryTopologicalSpaceWeaklyEquivalentToACWComplex"}
            #FactoringTopologicalCodiagonalThroughCylinder.num_example
              %h6#example_27 Example
              %p
                For
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in Top
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times I \longrightarrow X
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalInterval"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakHomotopyEquivalenceOfTopologicalSpaces"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\nabla_X
                      \\;\colon\;
                      X \sqcup X
                      \\stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow}
                      X\times I
                      \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                      X
              %p
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_X
                in def.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalInterval"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times I
              %p
                In fact, further below (prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardContractionOfStandardInterval"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sqcup X \to X \times I
                has better properties than the generic monomorphism has, in particular better homotopy invariant properties: it has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                against all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi p
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \stackrel{p}{\longrightarrow} B
                that are also
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            %p
              Of course the concept of left homotopy in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftHomotopy"}
              is accompanied by a concept of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+homotopy"} right homotopy
            #TopologicalPathSpace.num_defn
              %h6#definition_36 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"}> path space
                  )
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                %strong
                  standard topological
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
                is the topological
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
                = succeed "," do
