                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi X
                                %mi I
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      I \times X^I &amp;\overset{(t,\gamma)\mapsto \gamma(t\cdot(-))}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      X^I
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                To see that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^I \to X\times X
                is a fibration, we need to show that every commuting square of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
