              Moreover, compact generation fixes the associativity of the smash product (remark
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductOnTopNotAssociative"}
            #SmashProductInTopcgIsAssociative.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_40 Proposition
              %p
                On
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfPointedObjects"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductOfPointedObjects"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ×
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (-)\wedge (-)
                      \\;\colon\;
                      Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
                      \\times
                      Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
                      \\longrightarrow
                      Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
              %p
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                for it.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_65 Proof
              %p
                Since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\times X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                by prop.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianClosureOfTopcg"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                and in particular
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
                projections. Therefore with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, Z \in Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
                then
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi Z
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi X
                                      %mo ×
                                      %mi Y
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi X
                                      %mo ×
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                      %mi y
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                      %mo ⊔
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                      %mo ×
                                      %mi Y
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi Z
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ∧
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                  %mi z
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                  %mo ⊔
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                  %mo =
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mi y
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi Z
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                              %mfrac
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi Y
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi Z
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                    %mi y
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi Z
                                    %mo ⊔
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi Y
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi Z
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                  %mi z
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi Z
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ∨
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mo ∨
                                  %mi Z
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      (X \wedge Y) \wedge Z
                      \&amp; =
                      \\frac{
                      \\frac{X\times Y}{X \times\{y\} \sqcup \{x\}\times Y}
                      \\times Z
                      }{ (X \wedge Y)\times \{z\} \sqcup \{[x] = [y]\} \times Z}
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \simeq
                      \\frac{\frac{X \times Y \times Z}{X \times \{y\}\times Z \sqcup \{x\}\times Y \times Z}}{
                      X \times Y \times \{z\}
                      }
                      \\\
                      \&amp;\simeq
                      \\frac{X\times Y \times Z}{ X \vee Y \vee Z}
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,.
              %p
                The analogous reasoning applies to yield also
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi Z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Z
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∨
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ∨
                            %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \wedge (Y\wedge Z) \simeq \frac{X\times Y \times Z}{ X \vee Y \vee Z}
              %p
                The second statement follows directly with prop.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianClosureOfTopcg"}
            #PointedCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpacesIsSymmetricMonoidalClosed.num_remark
              %h6#remark_29 Remark
              %p
                Corollary
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashHomAdjunctionOnPointedCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
                together with prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashProductInTopcgIsAssociative"}
                says that under the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (Top_{cg}^{\ast/}, \wedge, S^0)
                      ,.
              %p
                Notice that by prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianClosureOfTopcg"}
                also unpointed compactly generated spaces under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                form a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (Top_{cg}, \times , \ast)
                      \\,.
              %p
                The fact that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
                is still closed symmetric monoidal but no longer Cartesian exhibits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
                as being “more
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                is the closed symmteric monoidal category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+spectra"} structured spectra
                under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
                which we discuss in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1"} section 1
            %p
              Due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotency
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \circ k \simeq k
              (cor.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              to it does not change it and one may continue working as in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            #CWComplexIsCompactlyGenerated.num_example
              %h6#example_36 Example
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated
            .proof
              %h6#proof_66 Proof
              %p
                Since
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+CW-complex+is+a+Hausdorff+space"} a CW-complex is a Hausdorff space
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffImpliessWeaklyHausdorff"}
                and prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacterizationOfCompactClosedSetsInWeaklyHausdorffSpace"}
                its
                = succeed "-closed" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspace"} compact subspace
                is closed.
              %p
                Since a CW-complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                over attachments of standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disks"} n-disks
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{n_i}
                (its cells), by the characterization of colimits in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                (
                %a{:href => "Top#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"}> prop.
                ) a subset of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is open or closed precisely if its restriction to each cell is open or closed, respectively. Since the
                = succeed "-disks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                intersected with all compact subsets is closed, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is closed.
              %p
                For the converse direction, since
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+CW-complex+is+a+Hausdorff+space"} a CW-complex is a Hausdorff space
                and since
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
            %p For completeness we record further classes of examples:
            .num_example
              %h6#example_37 Example
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                includes
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    all
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
                %li
                  %p
                    all
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-countable+topological+spaces"} first-countable topological spaces
                  %p hence in particular
                  %ol
                    %li
                      %p
                        all
                        = succeed "," do
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable+topological+spaces"} metrizable topological spaces
                    %li
                      %p
                        all
                        = succeed "," do
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+spaces"} discrete topological spaces
                    %li
                      %p
                        all
                        = succeed "." do
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+topological+spaces"} codiscrete topological spaces
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Lewis78"}> Lewis 78, p. 148
              )
            %p
              Recall that by corollary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              of compactly generated spaces are again compactly generated.
            #ProductOfCWWithLocallyCompactCWIsCompactlyGenerated.num_example
              %h6#example_38 Example
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                CW-complex, and more generally with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                CW-complex, is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "CW+complex#HatcherTopologyOfCellComplexes"}> Hatcher “Topology of cell complexes”, theorem A.6
              )
            %p More generally:
            #ProductOfCompactlyGeneratedWithLocallyCompactHausdorff.num_example
              %h6#proposition_41 Proposition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+space"} compactly generated space
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times Y
                is compactly generated.
            %p
              e.g. (
              %a{:href => "#Strickland09"}> Strickland 09, prop. 26
              )
            %p
              Finally we check that the concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              does not change under passing to compactly generated spaces:
            #kificationComparisonIsWeakHomotopyEquivalence.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_42 Proposition
              %p
                For every topological space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(X) \longrightarrow X
                (the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            .proof
              %h6#proof_67 Proof
              %p
                By example
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWComplexIsCompactlyGenerated"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfCWWithLocallyCompactCWIsCompactlyGenerated"}
                and lemma
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuousFunctionsOutOfCompactlyGeneratedFactorThroughCompactlyGeneratedClosureOfCodomain"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \to k(X)
                and their left homotopies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \times I \to k(X)
                are in bijection with functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \to X
                and their homotopies
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \times I \to X
            #ClassicalModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces.num_theorem
              %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
              %p
                The restriction of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
                from theorem
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
                along the inclusion
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg} \hookrightarrow Top
                of def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                is still a model category structure, which is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
                by the same sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingCofibrations"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrations"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenEquivalence"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                      %munderover
                        %mo ⊥
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi k
                        %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Quillen
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{k}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {\hookrightarrow}
                      {\bot}
                      Top_{Quillen}
                      \\,.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_68 Proof
              %p
                By example
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWComplexIsCompactlyGenerated"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
                are indeed in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(Top_{cg})
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfCWWithLocallyCompactCWIsCompactlyGenerated"}
                all arguments above about left homotopies between maps out of these basic cells go through verbatim in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JTopRelativeCellComplexesAreWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
                and lemma
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
                follows by general abstract arguments from these, it also still goes through verbatim for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                (repeatedly use the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"} retract argument
                to establish the two weak factorization systems).
              %p
                Hence the (acyclic) cofibrations in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top_{cg})_{Quillen}
                are identified with those in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi Quillen
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                (def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunction"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenEquivalence"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a compactly generated space then a continuous function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakHomotopyEquivalenceOfTopologicalSpaces"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f \colon X \to k(Y)
                is a weak homotopy equivalence. But, by lemma
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuousFunctionsOutOfCompactlyGeneratedFactorThroughCompactlyGeneratedClosureOfCodomain"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
                is the same function as
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kificationComparisonIsWeakHomotopyEquivalence"}
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              %strong Compactly generated weakly Hausdorff topological spaces
            %p
              While the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg} \hookrightarrow Top
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
              does satisfy the requirement that it gives a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              with all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              and containing all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            %p
              A popular choice introduced in (
              %a{:href => "weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space#McCord69"}> McCord 69
              ) is to add the further restriction to topopological spaces which are not only compactly generated but also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "compactly+generated+topological+space#Steenrod67"} Steenrod 67
              = succeed "))" do
                %a{:href => "weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space#McCord69"} McCord 69, section 2
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+spaces"} quotient spaces
            %p
              On the other hand, in above we wouldn’t have imposed Hausdorffness in the first place. More intrinsic advantages of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cgwH
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cgwH}
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
              are the following:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  of a morphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cgwH
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cgwH} \hookrightarrow Top
                  along a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
                  inclusion in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                  is again in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cgwH
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cgwH}
              %li
                %p
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cgwH
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cgwH}
                  quotient spaces are not only preserved by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+products"} cartesian products
                  (as is the case for all compactly generated spaces due to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times (-)
                  being a left adjoint, according to cor.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %li
                %p
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cgwH
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cgwH}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
                  are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
                  inclusions
            %p We will not need this here or in the following sections, but we briefly mention it for completenes:
            #WeaklyHausdorff.num_defn
              %h6#definition_55 Definition
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is called
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff
                if for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; K \longrightarrow X
              %p
                out of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(K) \subset X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            #HausdorffImpliessWeaklyHausdorff.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_43 Proposition
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+space"} weakly Hausdorff space
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeaklyHausdorff"}
            .proof
              %h6#proof_69 Proof
              %p
                Since
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
            #CharacterizationOfCompactClosedSetsInWeaklyHausdorffSpace.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_44 Proposition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff topological space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeaklyHausdorff"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
                is
                = succeed "-closed," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset X
                that is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspace"} compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
                with respect to the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cap A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              e.g. (
              %a{:href => "#Strickland09"}> Strickland 09, lemma 1.4 (c)
              )
            %h3#TopologicalEnrichment Topological enrichment
            %p
              So far the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              which we established in theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+functors"} projective model structures on topologically enriched functors
              induced from it in theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopologicalFunctors"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopEnrichedCategory"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunctions"} Quillen adjunctions
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#TheSuspensionLoopingDiscussion"} below
            #PushoutProduct.num_defn
              %h6#definition_56 Definition
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 \colon X_1 \to Y_1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2 \colon X_2 \to Y_2
                be morphisms in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo □
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      i_1\Box i_2
                      \\coloneqq
                      ((id, i_2), (i_1,id))
              %p is the universal morphism in the following diagram
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo ,
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi po
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %munder
                                %mo ⊔
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ×
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo ,
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; X_1 \times X_2
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{(i_1,id)}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{(id,i_2)}}
                      \\\
                      Y_1 \times X_2 &amp;&amp; (po) &amp;&amp; X_1 \times Y_2
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; (Y_1 \times X_2) \underset{X_1 \times X_2}{\sqcup} (X_1 \times Y_2)
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{((id, i_2), (i_1,id))}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; Y_1 \times Y_2
                      }
            #PushoutProductOfTwoInclusions.num_example
              %h6#example_39 Example
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 \colon X_1 \hookrightarrow Y_1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2 \colon X_2 \hookrightarrow Y_2
                are inclusions, then their pushout product
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo □
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 \Box i_2
                from def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProduct"}
                is the inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 2
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∪
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left(
                      X_1 \times Y_2 \;\cup\; Y_1 \times X_2
                      \\right)
                      \\hookrightarrow
                      Y_1 \times Y_2
                      \\,.
              %p For instance
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi I
                        %mo )
                      %mo □
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi I
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left(
                      \\{0\} \hookrightarrow I
                      \\right)
                      \\Box
                      \\left(
                      \\{0\} \hookrightarrow I
                      \\right)
              %p is the inclusion of two adjacent edges of a square into the square.
            #PushoutProductWithInitialMorphism.num_example
              %h6#example_40 Example
              %p
                The pushout product with an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
                morphism is just the ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                functor
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo □
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\emptyset \to X) \Box (-)
                      \\simeq
                      X \times (-)
                      \\,,
              %p i.e.
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
