            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"}> Piacenza 91, theorem 5.4
              )
            .proof
              %h6#proof_78 Proof
              %p
                By prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicallyEnrichedCopresheavesHaveAllLimitsAndColimits"}
                the category has all limits and colimits, hence it remains to check the model structure
              %p
                But via the enriched Yoneda lemma (prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicallyEnrichedYonedaLemma"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopQuillenModelStructure"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JTopRelativeCellComplexesAreWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
                and
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
                generalize immediately to the present situation, with the evident small change of wording:
              %p
                For instance, the fact that a morphism of topologically enriched functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon F \to G
                that has the right lifting property against the elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi I
                        %mi Top
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Top}^{\mathcal{C}}
                is a projective weak equivalence, follows by noticing that for fixed
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon F \to G
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"} enriched Yoneda lemma
                prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicallyEnrichedYonedaLemma"}
                gives a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                of commuting diagrams (and their fillers) of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi F
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi id
                                      %mo ⋅
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ι
                                        %mi n
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi η
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msup
                                  %mi D
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi G
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ↔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi η
                                        %mi c
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi D
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi G
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left(
                      \\array{
                      y(c) \cdot S^{n-1} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; F
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{(id\cdot \iota_n)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\eta}}
                      \\\
                      y(c) \cdot D^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; G
                      }
                      \\right)
                      \\;\;\;\leftrightarrow\;\;\;
                      \\left(
                      \\array{
                      S^{n-1} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; F(c)
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\eta_c}}
                      \\\
                      D^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; G(c)
                      }
                      \\right)
                      \\,,
              %p
                and hence the statement follows with part A) of the proof of lemma
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicSerreFibrationsAreTheJTopFibrations"}
              %p
                With these three lemmas in hand, the remaining formal part of the proof goes through verbatim as
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a{:href => "#VerificationOfTopQuillen"} above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
                (prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallObjectArgument"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"} retract argument
                (prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractArgument"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
                is evident.)
            #PreExcisiveFunctors.num_example
              %h6#example_44 Example
              %p
                Given examples
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopkAsATopologicallyEnrichedCategory"}
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicallyEnrichedFunctorsToTopk"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched category
                besides
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
                itself is the functor category
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [Top_{cg}^{\ast/}, Top_{cg}^{\ast/}]
                      \\,.
              %p
                The only technical problem with this is that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
                is not a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                (it has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
                of objects), which means that the existence of all limits and colimits via prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicallyEnrichedCopresheavesHaveAllLimitsAndColimits"}
                may (and does) fail.
              %p
                But so we just restrict to a small topologically enriched subcategory. A good choice is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mi cg
                          %mo ,
                          %mi fin
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ↪
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Top^{\ast/}_{cg,fin} \hookrightarrow Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
              %p
                of topological spaces homoemorphic to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complexes"} finite CW-complexes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopologicalFunctors"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mi cg
                          %mo ,
                          %mi fin
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [Top_{cg,fin}^{\ast/}\;,\; (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}]_{proj}
              %p
                is also also known as the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    strict
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                of the terminology “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+functors"}> n-excisive functors
                ” as used in “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"}> Goodwillie calculus
                ”, a homotopy-theoretic analog of
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+calculus"} differential calculus
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
                to a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+spectra"} model structure for spectra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2"} part 1.2
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#OnPreExcisiveFunctors"} on pre-excisive functors
            %p
              One consequence of theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopologicalFunctors"}
              is the model category theoretic incarnation of the theory of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            %p
              Observe that ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Limits"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
