            %p
              By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnNSequencesOfTopologicalSpaces"}
              it is immediate that the operation of forming colimits sends projective (acyclic) cofibrations between sequences of topological spaces to (acyclic) cofibrations in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusion, but a plain relative cell complex inclusion, more is true:
            #PropertiesOfColimitOverSequencesOfRelativeCellComplexes.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_52 Proposition
              %p
                In the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+functors"} projective model structures
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotowers"} cotowers
                in topological spaces,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
