                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+categories"} cofibrantly generated model categories
                (theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfPointedTopologicalSpaces"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomains"} codomains
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
                says that every morphism out of the domain or codomain of a generating acyclic cofibration into this colimit factors through a finite stage inclusion. Since a projective fibration is a degreewise fibration, we have the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                at that finite stage, and hence also the lifting property against the morphisms of colimits.
              %p Regarding the second statement:
              %p
                This is a model category theoretic version of a standard fact of plain
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                of sets,
                %a{:href => "commutativity+of+limits+and+colimits#FilteredColimitsCommuteWithFiniteLimits"} filtered colimits commute with finite limits
                in that there is an isomorphism of sets of the form which we have to prove is a weak homotopy equivalence of topological spaces. But now using that weak homotopy equivalences are detected by forming
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyGroupsOftopologicalSpaces"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
                out of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spheres"} spheres
                are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"}
                says that homming out of
                = succeed "-spheres" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
                (every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+functor"} hom functor
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
                in the second variable). Therefore we find isomorphisms of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
