            %p
              Kan complexes serve as a standard powerful model on which the complete formulation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              (without geometry) may be formulated.
            %h3#simplicial_sets Simplicial sets
            %p
              The concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              is secretly well familiar already in basic
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complexes"} singular simplicial complexes
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %p
              Conversely, every simplicial set may be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometrically realized
              as a topological space. These two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint"} adjoint
              operations turn out to exhibit the homotopy theory of simplicial sets as being equivalent (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"}> Quillen equivalent
              ) to the homotopy theory of topological spaces. For some purposes, working in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
              is preferable over working with topological homotopy theory.
            #TopologicalSimplex.num_defn
              %h6#definition_64 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+simplex"}> topological simplex
                  )
              %p
                For
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                %strong
                  %a{:href => "simplex#TopologicalSimplex"} topological n-simplex
                is, up to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                whose underlying set is the subset
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %munderover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi and
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi i
                      %mo .
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Delta^n \coloneqq
                      \\{
                      \\vec x \in \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
                      |
                      \\sum_{i = 0 }^n x_i = 1 \; and \;
                      \\forall i . x_i \geq 0
                      \\}
                      \\subset \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
              %p
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
                induces from the canonical topology in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
            .num_example
              %h6#example_46 Example
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                this is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0 = *
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                this is the standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1 = [0,1]
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                this is the filled triangle.
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
                this is the filled tetrahedron.
            #FaceInclusionInBarycentricCoords.num_defn
              %h6#definition_65 Definition
              %p
                For
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \n \geq 1
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \leq n
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  th
                  = succeed "-face" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                of the topological
                = succeed "-simplex," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta_k : \Delta^{n-1} \hookrightarrow \Delta^n
              %p
                induced under the coordinate presentation of def.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^n \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
              %p
                which “omits” the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (x_0, \cdots , x_{n-1}) \mapsto (x_0, \cdots, x_{k-1} , 0 , x_{k}, \cdots, x_n)
                      \\,.
            .num_example
              %h6#example_47 Example
              %p The inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta_0 : \Delta^0 \to \Delta^1
              %p is the inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ↪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\{1\} \hookrightarrow [0,1]
              %p of the “right” end of the standard interval. The other inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta_1 : \Delta^0 \to \Delta^1
              %p
                is that of the “left” end
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ↪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\} \hookrightarrow [0,1]
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/faceanddegeneracymaps.jpg", :width => "500"}/
            %p
              (graphics taken from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+set#Friedman08"} Friedman 08
            #DegeneracyProjectionsInBarycentricCoords.num_defn
              %h6#definition_66 Definition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \lt n
                the
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  th degenerate
                  = succeed "-simplex" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n)
                is the surjective map
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\sigma_k : \Delta^{n} \to \Delta^{n-1}
              %p
                induced under the barycentric coordinates of def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
                under the surjection
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{n+1} \to \mathbb{R}^n
              %p which sends
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (x_0, \cdots, x_n) \mapsto (x_0, \cdots, x_{k} + x_{k+1}, \cdots, x_n)
                      \\,.
            #SingularSimplex.num_defn
              %h6#definition_67 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplex"}> singular simplex
                  )
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                %strong
                  singular
                  = succeed "-simplex" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\sigma : \Delta^n \to X
              %p
                from the topological
                = succeed "-simplex," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %p Write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (Sing X)_n \coloneqq Hom_{Top}(\Delta^n , X)
              %p
                for the set of singular
                = succeed "-simplices" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/singularsimplices.jpg", :width => "500"}/
            %p
              (graphics taken from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+set#Friedman08"} Friedman 08
            %p
              The sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sing X)_\bullet
              here are closely related by an interlocking system of maps that make them form what is called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingularSimplicialComplex"}
            %p
              Since the topological
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
              sit inside each other by the face inclusions of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FaceInclusionInBarycentricCoords"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_k : \Delta^{n-1} \to \Delta^{n}
            %p
              and project onto each other by the degeneracy maps, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegeneracyProjectionsInBarycentricCoords"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_k : \Delta^{n+1} \to \Delta^n
            %p we dually have functions
