                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardCosimplicialTopologicalSpace"}
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+functor"} hom functor
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (Sing X) : [n] \mapsto Hom_{Top}( \Delta^n , X )
                      \\,.
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_35 Remark
              %p
                It turns out – this is the content of the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"}> homotopy hypothesis
                  \-theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67
                ) – that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                of the topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is entirely captured by its singular simplicial complex
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sing
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing X
