                this morphism has an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
                through the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi Λ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo +
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↗
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi θ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Lambda^{n+1}[n] &amp; \longrightarrow &amp; X
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\theta}}
                      \\\
                      \\Delta[n+1]
                      }
              %p
                From the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
                one finds that the boundary of the
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
                is constant on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mi θ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi i
                      %mi θ
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      d_i d_{n} \theta = d_{n-1} d_i \theta = x
              %p
                So
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
                represents an element in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
                and we define a product operation on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
                by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [f]\cdot [g] \coloneqq [d_n \theta]
                      \\,.
            %p
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"} Goerss-Jardine 99, p. 26
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_36 Remark
              %p
                All the degenerate
                = succeed "-simplices" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_{0 \leq i \leq n-2}
                in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
                are just there so that the gluing of the two
                = succeed "-cells" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                to each other can be regarded as forming the boundary of an
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi n
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            .num_lemma
              %h6#lemma_25 Lemma
              %p
                The product on homotopy group elements in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
                is well defined, in that it is independent of the choice of representatives
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                and of the extension
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            %p
              e.g. (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, lemma 7.1
              )
            .num_lemma
              %h6#lemma_26 Lemma
              %p
                The product operation in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
                yields a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                structure on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            %p
              e.g. (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, theorem 7.2
              )
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_37 Remark
              %p
                The first homotopy group,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X,x)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            #WeakHomotopyEquivalence.num_defn
              %h6#definition_75 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                  of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi KanCplx
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in KanCplx \hookrightarrow sSet
                two
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              %p
                is called a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                if it induces
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                on all
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial homotopy groups
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⟶
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f) \colon \pi_0(X) \longrightarrow \pi_0(Y)
                    is a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                    of sets;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⟶
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(f,x) \colon \pi_n(X,x) \longrightarrow \pi_n(Y,f(x))
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                    for all
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X_0
                    and all
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            %h3#KanComplexes Kan complexes
            %p
              Recall the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              from
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#SingularSimplicialSet"} above
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Simp
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta[n] = \mathbf{\Delta}( -, [n]) \in  Simp Set
            %p
              be the standard simplicial
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SimpSet
            #SimplicialHorn.num_defn
              %h6#definition_76 Definition
              %p
                For each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq i \leq n
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,i)
                  \-horn
                or
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,i)
                  \-box
                is the subsimplicial set
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Lambda^i[n]
                      \\hookrightarrow
                      \\Delta[n]
              %p
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                of all faces
                %em except
                the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mi th
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^{th}
                one.
              %p
                This is called an
                %strong outer horn
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong inner horn
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark_38 Remark
              %p
                Since
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                make sense and they are calculated objectwise, thus in this case dimensionwise. This way it becomes clear what the structure of a horn as a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^k[n]: \Delta^{op} \to Set
                must therefore be: it takes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m]
                to the collection of ordinal maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: [m] \to [n]
                which do not have the element
