                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated topological space
                if each of its compactly closed subspaces is already closed.
              %p Write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Top_{cg} \hookrightarrow Top
              %p
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                on the compactly generated topological spaces.
            %p
              Often the condition is added that a compactly closed topological space be also a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff topological space
            #ExamplesOfCompactlyGeneratedTopologiclSpaces.num_example
              %h6#example_66 Example
              %p
                Examples of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    every
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
                %li
                  %p
                    every
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact space
                %li
                  %p
                    every
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
                %li
                  %p
                    every
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                %li
                  %p
                    every
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+countable+space"} first countable space
            #TopologicalRealizationOfSSetLandsInkTop.num_cor
              %h6#corollary_10 Corollary
              %p
                The topological
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                functor of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                in example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
                takes values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      {\vert - \vert}
                      \\;\colon\;
                      sSet
                      \\longrightarrow Top_{cg}
            .proof
              %h6#proof_93 Proof
              %p
                By example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfCompactlyGeneratedTopologiclSpaces"}
                and prop.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfsSetLandsInCWComplexes"}
            #kTopIsCoreflectiveInTop.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_68 Proposition
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg} \hookrightarrow Top
                of def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                has the following properties
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    It is a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mi cg
                          %mover
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mi k
                            %mo ↪
                          %mi Top
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          Top_{cg} \stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\underset{k}{\longleftarrow}} Top
                          \\,.
                  %p
                    The coreflection
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(X)
                    of a topological space is given by adding to the open subsets of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    all compactly open subsets, def.
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTop"}
                %li
                  %p
                    It has all small
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                  %p
                    The colimits are computed in
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Top
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                    of the limits as computed in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Top
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                %li
                  %p
                    It is a
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
                  %p
                    The
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
                    in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Top
                            %mi cg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                    is the image under
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                    of the Cartesian product formed in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Top
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            %p
              This is due to (
              %a{:href => "compactly+generated+topological+space#Steenrod67"}> Steenrod 67
              ), expanded on in (
              %a{:href => "compactly+generated+topological+space#Lewis78"}> Lewis 78, appendix A
              ). One says that prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveInTop"}
              with example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfCompactlyGeneratedTopologiclSpaces"}
              makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
              a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"}> convenient category of topological spaces
              ”.
            #Timesk.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_69 Proposition
              %p
                Regarded, via corollary
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSSetLandsInkTop"}
                as a functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert - \vert} \colon sSet \to Top_{cg}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            %p
              See at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "geometric+realization#GeometricRealizationIsLeftExact"} Geometric realization is left exact
            .proof
              %h6#proof_idea_3 Proof idea
              %p
                The key step in the proof is to use the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closure
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                (prop.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kTopIsCoreflectiveInTop"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                and hence preserves colimits in each variable, so that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
                in the definition of the geometric realization may be taken out of Cartesian products.
            .num_lemma
              %h6#lemma_32 Lemma
              %p
                The
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+Kan+fibration"} minimal Kan fibration
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinimalKanFibration"}
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
            %p
              This is due to (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"}> Gabriel-Zisman 67
              ). See for instance (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, chapter I, corollary 10.8, theorem 10.9
              ).
            .proof
              %h6#proof_idea_4 Proof idea
              %p
                By prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinimalKanFibrationAreFiberBundles"}
                minimal Kan fibrations are simplicial
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Timesk"}
                this property translates to their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                also being a locally trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
            #GeometricRealizationOfKanFibrationIsSerreFibration.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_70 Proposition
              %p
                The
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanFibration"}
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
            %p
              This is due to (
              %a{:href => "Kan+fibration#Quillen68"}> Quillen 68
              ). See for instance (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, chapter I, theorem 10.10
              ).
            #UnitOfSingularNerveAndRealizationIsWEOnKanComplexes.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_71 Proposition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} unit
                of the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                (prop.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NerveAndRealizationAdjunction"}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Sing
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      S \longrightarrow Sing {\vert S \vert}
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakHomotopyEquivalence"}
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi Sing
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      {\vert Sing X\vert} \longrightarrow X
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %p
              e.g. (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, chapter I, prop. 11.1 and p. 63
              ).
            .proof
              %h6#proof_idea_5 Proof idea
              %p
                Use prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingDetextsAndReflectsFibrations"}
                and prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeometricRealizationOfKanFibrationIsSerreFibration"}
                applied to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+fibration"} path fibration
                to proceed by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %h3#the_classical_model_structure_on_simplicial_sets The classical model structure on simplicial sets
            #ClassesOfMorphismsOnsSetQuillen.num_defn
              %h6#definition_91 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"}> classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  )
              %p
                The classical model structure on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Quillen
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    The classical
                    %strong weak equivalences
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                    are the morphisms whose
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                    of
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                %li
                  %p
                    The classical
                    %strong fibrations
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                    are the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %strong
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanFibration"}
                %li
                  %p
                    The classical
                    %strong cofibrations
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                    are the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                    of simplicial sets, i.e. the degreewise
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
            .num_prop
              %h6#proposition_72 Proposition
              %p
                In model structure
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Quillen
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorphismsOnsSetQuillen"}
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    The fibrant objects are precisely the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                %li
                  %p
                    A morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo :
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                    of fibrant simplicial sets /
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                    is a weak equivalence precisely if it induces an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    on all
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial homotopy groups
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnderlyingSetsOfSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
                %li
                  %p All simplicial sets are cofibrant with respect to this model structure.
            .num_prop
              %h6#proposition_73 Proposition
              %p
                The
                %strong acyclic fibrations
                in
                = succeed "(i.e." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Quillen
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                are precisely the morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                that have the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                with respect to all inclusions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[n] \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
                of boundaries of
                = succeed "-simplices" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "-simplices" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mo ∃
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mi f
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\partial \Delta[n] &amp;\to&amp; X
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;{}^\exists\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^f
                      \\\
                      \\Delta[n] &amp;\to&amp; Y
                      }
                      \\,.
            %p
              This appears spelled out for instance as (
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GoerssJardine99"}> Goerss-Jardine 99, theorem 11.2
              ).
            %p In fact:
            .num_prop
              %h6#proposition_74 Proposition
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                with
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    generating cofibrations the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                    inclusions
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo →
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[n] \to \Delta[n]
                %li
                  %p
                    generating acyclic cofibrations the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
                    inclusions
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo →
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^i[n] \to \Delta[n]
            .num_theorem
              %h6#theorem_7 Theorem
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                be the smallest class of morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                satisfying the following conditions:
              %ol
                %li
                  The class of monomorphisms that are in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is closed under
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
                  property in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi sSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                  and contains all the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                %li
                  For all natural numbers
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta [n] \to \Delta [0]
                  is in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %p
                Then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                is the class of weak homotopy equivalences.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_94 Proof
              %ul
                %li
                  First, notice that the horn inclusions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^0 [1] \hookrightarrow \Delta [1]
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^1 [1] \hookrightarrow \Delta [1]
                  are in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %li
                  Suppose that the horn inclusion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^k [m] \hookrightarrow \Delta [m]
                  is in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \lt n
                  and all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi k
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi m
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \le k \le m
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi l
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \le l \le n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^l [n] \hookrightarrow \Delta [n]
                  is also in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %li
                  Quillen’s
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
                  then implies all the trivial cofibrations are in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
                  is a trivial Kan fibration, then its right lifting property implies there is a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : Y \to X
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \circ s = id_Y
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : Y \to X
                  is a trivial cofibration. Thus every trivial Kan fibration is also in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %li
                  Every weak homotopy equivalence factors as
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \circ i
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a trivial Kan fibration and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  is a trivial cofibration, so every weak homotopy equivalence is indeed in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %li
                  Finally, noting that the class of weak homotopy equivalences satisfies the conditions in the theorem, we deduce that it is the
                  %em smallest
                  such class.
            %p
              As a corollary, we deduce that the classical model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              is the smallest (in terms of weak equivalences) model structure for which the cofibrations are the monomorphisms and the weak equivalences include the (combinatorial) homotopy equivalences.
            .num_prop
              %h6#proposition_75 Proposition
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 : sSet \to Set
                be the connected components functor, i.e. the left adjoint of the constant functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cst
                        %mo :
                        %mi Set
                        %mo →
                        %mi sSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cst : Set \to sSet
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Z \to W
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                is a weak homotopy equivalence if and only if the induced map
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 K^f : \pi_0 K^W \to \pi_0 K^Z
              %p
                is a bijection for all
                %em Kan complexes
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            .proof
              %h6#proof_95 Proof
              %p
                One direction is easy: if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialModelCategory"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{(-)} : sSet^{op} \to sSet
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"} Ken Brown's lemma
                (Prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KenBrownLemma"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 K^{(-)} : sSet^{op} \to Set
                sends weak homotopy equivalences to bijections.
              %p
                Conversely, when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is a Kan complex, there is a natural bijection between
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 K^X
                and the hom-set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho (sSet) (X, K)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Z \to W
                such that the induced morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 K^W \to \pi_0 K^Z
                is a bijection for all Kan complexes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is precisely a morphism that becomes an isomorphism in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho (sSet)
            #TopsSetQuillenEquivalence.num_theorem
              %h6#theorem_8 Theorem
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                  between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              %p
                The
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} adjunction
                of example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfSimplicialSets"}
                constitutes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                between the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
                of def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorphismsOnsSetQuillen"}
                and the
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi Sing
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Quillen
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mi Q
                          %msub
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Q
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Sing
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ({\vert -\vert}\dashv Sing)
                      \\;\colon\;
                      Top_{Quillen}
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{Sing}{\longrightarrow}}
                      {\overset{{\vert -\vert}}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {\phantom{{}_{Q}}\simeq_{Q}}
                      sSet_{Quillen}
            .proof
              %h6#proof_96 Proof
              %p
                First of all, the adjunction is indeed a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingDetextsAndReflectsFibrations"}
                says in particular that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sing
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing(-)
                takes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
                to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
                and prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRealizationOfsSetLandsInCWComplexes"}
                gives that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert-\vert}
                sends monomorphisms of simplicial sets to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              %p
                Now prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnitOfSingularNerveAndRealizationIsWEOnKanComplexes"}
                says that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+counit"} derived adjunction counit
                are weak equivalences, and hence the Quillen adjunction is a Quillen equivalence.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %div
            %h2#basic_notions_of_higher_topos_theory Basic notions of higher topos theory
            %p
              We have discussed basic notions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
              %a{:href => "#BasicNotionsOfToposTheory"} above
              and of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "#BasicNotionsOfHomotopyTheory"}> above
              ). The combination of the two is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} higher topos theory
              which we discuss here.
            %p
              We had explained how
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
              may be thought of as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
              and how
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              is about relaxing the concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
              to that of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              and
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformation"} higher gauge transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopy"} higher homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} higher toposes
              may be thought of as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} higher categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
              whose probe are defined only up to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            %p (…)
            %h3#LocallyPresentbableInfinityCategories
              Locally presentable
              = succeed "-Categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p
              The analog of the notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyPresentableCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CombinatorialModelCategory"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrant generation
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}
              below) in that all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of
              = succeed "-inclusions." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
            %p
              That this is indeed the correct
              = succeed "-analog" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
              is the statement of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DuggerTheorem"}
              below).
            %p
              Hence as we pass to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"} localization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
              at the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy-theoretic
              refinement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PrCat"} PrCat
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoCombModCat"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
              we also refer to as a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
              we also refer to as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
              of an
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"}> (∞,1)-colimit
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserving
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            #CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"}> cofibrantly generated model category
                  )
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
                %strong cofibrantly generated
                if there exists two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ,
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      I, J \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
              %p
                of its class of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                    have small domains according to def.
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassOfMorphismsWithSmallDomains"}
                %li
                  %p
                    the (acyclic) cofibrations of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    are precisely the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi I
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
                    (
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                    \-relative cell complexes), def.
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCCellComplex"}
            #CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategoryLifting.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                ), then its classes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Fib
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Cof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W, Fib, Cof
                of weak equivalences, fibrations and cofibrations are equivalently expressed as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+or+projective+morphisms"} injective or projective morphisms
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingAndExtension"}
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cof
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mi Inj
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof = (I Inj) Proj
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Fib
                          %mo =
                          %mi I
                          %mi Inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Fib = I Inj
                    ;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi Cof
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi J
                          %mi Inj
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Cof = (J Inj) Proj
                    ;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Fib
                          %mo =
                          %mi J
                          %mi Inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib = J Inj
                    ;
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p
                It is clear from the definition that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mi Inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset (I Inj) Proj
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
                gives an inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cof
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mi Inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Proj
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Cof \subset (I Inj) Proj
                      \\,.
              %p
                For the converse inclusion, let
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mi Inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in (I Inj) Proj
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallObjectArgument"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                            %mi Cell
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi I
                            %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \overset{\in I Cell}{\longrightarrow}\overset{I Inj}{\longrightarrow}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"} retract argument
                lemma
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractArgument"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is a retract of an
                = succeed "-relative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cof
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof
              %p
                This proves the first statement. Together with the closure properties of prop.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
              %p
                The proof of the third and fourth item is directly analogous, just with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                replaced for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            #CombinatorialModelCategory.num_defn
              %h6#definition_2 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"}> combinatorial model category
                  )
              %p
                A
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
                    (Def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyPresentableCategory"}
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                    (Def.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}
            #ClassicalModelStructureOnSimplicialSetsIsCombinatorial.num_prop
              %h6#example Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  is
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorphismsOnsSetQuillen"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Qu
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
                (Def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CombinatorialModelCategory"}
            #CategoriesOfSimplicialPresheaves.num_example
              %h6#example_2 Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+presheaves"}> category of simplicial presheaves
                  )
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallCategory"}
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                (Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopEnrichedCategory"}
                with Example
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfCosmoi"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+presheaf+category"} enriched presheaf category
                (Example
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EnrichedPresheaf"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      sPSh(\mathcal{C})
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      [\mathcal{C}^{op}, sSet]
              %p
                This is called the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+presheaves"} category of simplicial presheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %p
                By Prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialSetsAsPresheavesOnTheSimplexCategory"}
                this is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointEquivalenceOfCategories"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
                in the
