                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunction"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategoriesOfSimplicialPresheaves"}
                this is the case before
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
                (by Prop.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialPresheavesIsProperCombinatorialSimplicial"}
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RecognitionOfSimplicialQuillenAdjunction"}
                it is sufficient to check that the right Quillen functor preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfLeftBousfieldLocalization"}
                this means to check that it preserves
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
                is assumed to be projectively cofibrant, and since injectively fibrant objects are already projectively fibrant, the condition on an injectively local object according to Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivedLocalObjects"}
                is exactly the same as for a projectively local object.
              %p
                Now to see that this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
                induce an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategoriesOfSimplicialPresheaves"}
                this is the case before
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfLeftBousfieldLocalization"}
                it is thus sufficient to check that derived functors (before localization) preserves
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComputationOfLeftRightDerivedFunctorsViaResolutions"}
                for this it is sufficient that the Quillen functors themselves preserve local objects. For the right Quillen functor we have just seen this in the previous paragaraph, for the left Quillen functor it follows analogously.
